# TanStack Table philosophy

Headless, UI-agnostic. It ships logic, not markup/CSS. You bring the components (great with shadcn/ui, Tailwind, Radix, MUI, etc.).

Framework-agnostic core. One core, adapters for React/Svelte/Solid/Vue. Same mental model everywhere.

Controlled state first. Sorting, filtering, pagination, selection, column vis/resize, etc. are your state. The table exposes models & helpers; you decide where state lives (local, Redux, Zustand, URL, server).

Data in → models out. Pure, memoized calculations (row model, column model). Minimal re-renders, stable refs, and predictable performance.

Opt-in features. Small core; add only what you need. Tree-shakeable and composable.

Type-safety as a feature. Strong TS generics for rows, accessors, and column defs; catches config/renderer mistakes at compile time.

Server-friendly. It doesn’t fetch. You can do server-side sorting/filtering/pagination easily (pairs naturally with TanStack Query or your own data layer).

Composable, not monolithic. Hooks/utilities instead of a “god component.” You assemble tables, grids, and complex layouts from primitives.

Performance-focused. Encourages virtualization (via @tanstack/react-virtual), memoized accessors, and fine-grained updates.

Examples ≠ API. The examples are just patterns; the library avoids opinionated behaviors so you can match your design system and a11y strategy.
